From c2d23c64b7f71864c5fc16abde4d1bc8b0582b4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:24:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fork: voice mode shows agent status in a panel tab, mic state
 in the strip
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Muting used to replace the agent's Thinking/Speaking label, because one
resolver returned a single status and muted won over every phase. Human and
agent state now render separately.

- PanelTab: a design-system tab that peeks from behind a panel (one SVG
  outline with concave base flares; hidden/compact/expanded; slow
  ease-in-out rise, sink and resize; reduced motion). /design/panel-tab and
  a catalog entry.
- ShapeMorph: any-preset-to-any-preset outline morph (orbit, bars, ring,
  dot, ellipsis, lineup), Skia on native and SVG on web (no CanvasKit on
  web), shared worklet-safe shape model with tests. /design/shape-morph and
  a catalog entry.
- VolumeMeter mode think|live: orbit while the agent thinks, morphing into
  the live bars and handing off to the device-pixel-snapped bars.
- Voice mode: resolveMicState + resolveAgentVoiceStatus replace
  resolveRealtimeVoiceStatusKey. The agent's status ("Claude · Thinking",
  "Claude · Speaking" with an avatar ring, compact avatar while waiting)
  lives in a centered PanelTab behind the composer card with its own polite
  live region. The strip shows only the mic toggle ("Mic on" / "Muted",
  aria-pressed), the Space hint and End. The jump-to-bottom button sits
  above the tab. Speaking uses agentPlaybackLevel (idle pulse until voice
  telemetry reports a playback level).
- i18n for all nine locales; worklet declaration-order rule in
  docs/coding-standards.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
