+# Panel tab
+
+## Problem
+
+In voice mode the strip carries both parties: your mic and the agent's status. On phone
+the agent chip truncates and crowds the mic toggle. The panel tab gives the agent its own
+place on the edge between the transcript and the composer, so the strip holds only your
+controls. This design covers the tab itself; `AgentVoiceTab`
+(`components/agent-voice-tab.tsx`) wires it into the composer, and `/design/voice-strip`
+shows it there. Spec: option F in `.dev/mockups/voice-status-split.html`.
+
+## States
+
+| State id    | When the user sees it                                    | What they can do                      |
+| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
+| `hidden`    | Voice is off. The tab is behind the card, the row closed | Nothing; the composer sits as today   |
+| `compact`   | The agent waits for you. Avatar only, sunk 6px           | Read who is on the line               |
+| `expanded`  | The agent thinks or speaks. Avatar plus label            | Read the agent's status               |
+| `lifecycle` | Loops rise, expanded, compact, expanded, sink            | Review the motion                     |
+| `composer`  | Expanded over a composer card with voice controls        | Check the tab against the card's edge |
+
+## Flow
+
+1. Voice starts: the row opens and the tab rises from `hidden` (860ms).
+2. The agent thinks or speaks: `expanded`; the label fades in after the tab widens.
+3. The agent waits: the label fades out, then the tab narrows and sinks to `compact` (680ms).
+4. Voice ends: the tab sinks to `hidden` (820ms) and the row closes.
+
+## Components
+
+`PanelTab` (`components/ui/panel-tab.tsx`) wraps the panel and takes `state`, `leading`
+and `label`. The outline, flares included, is one `react-native-svg` path rebuilt on the
+UI thread. The wrapper always renders so the panel never remounts; the tab mounts when it
+first leaves `hidden` and unmounts once it has sunk again. The avatar here is a stand-in;
+the composer's is local to `AgentVoiceTab`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Light theme status word: `foregroundMuted` on `surface2` is 4.40:1 in light, under AA
+  (4.5:1) for 12px text, so light uses `foreground`. Dark keeps `foregroundMuted` (5.82:1). `AgentVoiceTab`
+  applies it; this design's stand-in label does not.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Promote the avatar to a primitive if a second surface needs one.
